Exhaust with r=33.9 just 2 below FAR due steps; sampling stars fine. They are rays with minR 4-5, just lensed by hole. Good.

At boundary near shadow (`50,19` minR 2.18, r=25) samples stars, likely photon ring. Good.

So shader behavior: exhausted r>7 sample stars. This creates proper background around disk.

Need ensure for exhausted with r >7 but disk maybe crossed plane outside disk? no disk hit; fine. For r<7 and not captured, return black. The shadow boundary may have some r 3-7 exhausted rays that would eventually escape; blackening them slightly expands shadow. We could sample stars with fade based on r:
